{"title":"Career roadmap · Industrial Designer","role":"Industrial Designer","summary":"An Industrial Designer designs physical products by combining user needs, aesthetics, ergonomics, engineering constraints, materials, manufacturing processes, sustainability, and business requirements.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career alignment"},{"type":"p","text":"An Industrial Designer designs physical products by combining user needs, aesthetics, ergonomics, engineering constraints, materials, manufacturing processes, sustainability, and business requirements."},{"type":"p","text":"The role can cover consumer electronics, appliances, furniture, automotive products, medical devices, tools, packaging, mobility products, lifestyle products, industrial equipment, and emerging smart products."},{"type":"p","text":"A B.Des in Product / Industrial Design is directly aligned with this career. The strongest graduates combine design thinking + sketching + 3D CAD + prototyping + materials/manufacturing knowledge + user research + visualisation + AI-assisted design."},{"type":"note","label":"Important distinction","text":"An industrial designer focuses primarily on the form, function, usability, experience, and manufacturability of products. Engineering professionals may own detailed engineering calculations, structural validation, electronics, or manufacturing process design."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical Roles"],"rows":[[{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"Design Intern, Product Design Intern, Junior Industrial Designer"}],[{"text":"Early Career"},{"text":"Industrial Designer, Product Designer"}],[{"text":"Mid Career"},{"text":"Senior Industrial Designer, Product Design Lead"}],[{"text":"Advanced"},{"text":"Lead Industrial Designer, Design Manager"}],[{"text":"Leadership"},{"text":"Design Director, Head of Industrial Design"}],[{"text":"Entrepreneurship"},{"text":"Independent Product Designer / Design Studio Founder"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During the B.Des","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Design Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"The first year should establish strong visual and design fundamentals."},{"type":"h","text":"Design fundamentals"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design principles"},{"text":"Form and composition"},{"text":"Colour theory"},{"text":"Typography basics"},{"text":"Visual communication"},{"text":"Design history"},{"text":"Design culture"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Creative problem solving"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Drawing"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Freehand sketching"},{"text":"Perspective"},{"text":"Orthographic views"},{"text":"Product sketching"},{"text":"Exploded views"},{"text":"Concept sketching"},{"text":"Marker/rendering techniques"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Introduction to product design"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Product anatomy"},{"text":"Form development"},{"text":"Human interaction"},{"text":"Basic ergonomics"},{"text":"Materials"},{"text":"Manufacturing awareness"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project"},{"type":"h","text":"Everyday Product Redesign"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose a common product such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Water bottle"},{"text":"Backpack"},{"text":"Chair"},{"text":"Desk lamp"},{"text":"Kitchen tool"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Analyse:"},{"type":"flow","items":["User","Problem","Research","Concepts","Sketches","Prototype","Final Design"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Product Design + CAD"},{"type":"p","text":"The second year should develop technical product-design capabilities."},{"type":"h","text":"CAD"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn at least one professional 3D CAD workflow:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SolidWorks"},{"text":"Fusion"},{"text":"Rhino"},{"text":"Alias"},{"text":"Siemens NX"},{"text":"Creo"}]},{"type":"p","